From ef5db17e5a1aa0a8d4c3b3db375ce7ddf11ba8fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vince8x <vince.tran8x@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Aug 2024 16:24:27 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Implement support for Dogecoin addresses (#39)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

• Added DogeAddress struct and associated methods for handling Dogecoin addresses.
• Replaced CashAddress references with DogeAddress in API endpoints for transactions and address handling.
• Updated HTML templates to reflect the changes in address handling for Dogecoin.
• Temporary comment-out unused token address in template until address format is decided.

Co-authored-by: Tobias Ruck <ruck.tobias@gmail.com>

Original-Commit: f0084629da17e56b1588ebb28a9e36286b20b334
Adaptation: Keep current explorer token handling, scripts, malformed-script guards and templates while switching transaction destinations/search/address queries to Dogecoin Base58Check. Retain original DogeAddress implementation with corrected testnet P2PKH prefix and regtest P2SH support; network round-trip tests cover all six network/type combinations. Tokens share the native address, without inventing a token address encoding. Use root Cargo.lock after the upstream workspace consolidation.
Reference follow-up a18cc5365a917841b404b8e126fb1755ac4b1706 fixes old template variable names; current templates already use the correct sats fields and script-hex filters, retained here.

